{"topicSections":[{"title":"Sending to TelemetryDeck","anchor":"Sending-to-TelemetryDeck","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckSetupError"]},{"title":"Encoding batches","anchor":"Encoding-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder"]},{"title":"Records left out","anchor":"Records-left-out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckEncodingError"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Send records to TelemetryDeck as signals, through its Ingest API v3.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding"]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"TelemetryDeckEncoding","modules":[{"name":"TelemetryDeckEncoding"}],"symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework","title":"TelemetryDeckEncoding"},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"makes an "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":") for TelemetryDeck in one call. It checks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the app ID and your organization’s namespace, then posts to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"https:\/\/nom.telemetrydeck.com\/v3\/<namespace>\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". Each batch is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"split to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":": 100 signals a request, as TelemetryDeck’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftSDK sends them; 333,333 bytes a signal, a third of Ingest API v3’s limit of 1,000,000; and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1,000,000 bytes a request, the encoder’s own bound, as TelemetryDeck documents none. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no request. The destination retries no response, a 5xx (TelemetryDeck answers 503 while its queue"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is full), 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. No trace context is sent."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves this module out, so import it on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The app ID only says which app a signal belongs to, and TelemetryDeck’s own SDKs ship it inside"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every app, so the destination builds on every platform and an app sends to TelemetryDeck directly."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import TelemetryDeckEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let telemetryDeck = try HTTPDestination.telemetryDeck(","    appID: appID,  \/\/ from the app's settings in the TelemetryDeck dashboard","    namespace: \"com.example\",  \/\/ your organization's namespace","    testMode: false,  \/\/ true for builds whose signals only Test Mode should show","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: telemetryDeck)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The factory throws "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckSetupError","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for an app ID that is empty or only whitespace,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and for a namespace TelemetryDeck doesn’t take. A namespace holds only ASCII letters, digits, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"."},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":", and can’t be "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"w"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"."},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".."},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"testMode"},{"type":"text","text":" has no default. TelemetryDeck shows test signals only in its Test Mode, apart from your"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"real users, and its SDK picks test mode for debug builds. Pass whatever your app uses to tell its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"builds apart, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#if DEBUG"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":" otherwise."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"User counts are sessions","level":3,"anchor":"User-counts-are-sessions","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"TelemetryDeck counts users by ","type":"text"},{"code":"clientUser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The destination sends the record’s session, from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sessions enricher, as ","type":"text"},{"code":"clientUser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", hashed the way TelemetryDeck’s SDKs hash a user identifier:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SHA-256 of the lowercase UUID, in lowercase hex, with the SDKs’ default, empty salt.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"TelemetryDeck salts and hashes ","type":"text"},{"code":"clientUser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" again on its server. The same session is also the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"sessionID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in the clear, so a salt of the app’s own would hide nothing, and the destination takes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"none. Nothing else identifies a record: no vendor identifier, device identifier or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"account, and no trace context.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"So TelemetryDeck’s user counts are session counts. A person who opens the app three times is three","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"users, and its retention charts show how long a session lasts, not whether people come back. That","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is the library’s default, for privacy. To count devices instead, put","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"StandardContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s ","type":"text"},{"code":"VendorIdentifierKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the records’ context and send them through a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination that reads it, or write your own enricher and encoder that send the identifier you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"choose. This encoder sends the session alone.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record with no session, from a tracker without the sessions enricher, is its own user: its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"clientUser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the hash of the record’s identifier, and it has no ","type":"text"},{"code":"sessionID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A record a store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"recovered after a relaunch keeps its session, and with it the ","type":"text"},{"code":"clientUser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"sessionID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first send. Making up a session","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"would join unrelated records, and skipping the record would lose it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"What TelemetryDeck receives","level":3,"anchor":"What-TelemetryDeck-receives","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each request is a JSON array of signals, one per record. Every signal has:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appID"},{"text":", as given, without surrounding whitespace;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"type"},{"type":"text","text":", the event’s name;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"clientUser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the hashed session, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"sessionID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the session;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"receivedAt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the record’s timestamp in ISO 8601 with milliseconds, so a signal sent late still","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"counts at the time it was tracked;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"isTestMode","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"\"true\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"\"false\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":";"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.SDK.name"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"made with, and sit beside these, each keeping its JSON type. TelemetryDeck doesn’t index nested"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values, so an object or array is flattened into dotted names: a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cart"},{"type":"text","text":" holding "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"size"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cart.size"},{"type":"text","text":", and the first element of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tags"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tags.0"},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" property is left out. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"floatValue"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The standard context, when the record has it, becomes TelemetryDeck’s built-in parameters:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Context"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Parameters","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.AppInfo.version"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".buildNumber"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".versionAndBuildNumber"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"DeviceKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.Device.modelName"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"OperatingSystemKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.Device.operatingSystem"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".platform"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".systemVersion"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".systemMajorVersion"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".systemMajorMinorVersion"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocaleKey"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.RunContext.locale"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".language"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.UserPreference.region"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The bundle identifier, the form factor and the network aren’t sent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Records left out","level":3,"anchor":"Records-left-out","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose event name or parameter name, once flattened, holds anything but ASCII letters, digits,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"."},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"text":", or is empty. TelemetryDeck refuses the whole request for one such name.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name or parameter name starts with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck."},{"type":"text","text":", in any case: TelemetryDeck"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reserves that scope for its SDKs’ parameters and its server’s;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one with a parameter named as one of a signal’s own members, ","type":"text"},{"code":"appID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"clientUser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"receivedAt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"sessionID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"isTestMode","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"floatValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", spelled exactly so: in the flat","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"signal it would replace the member. A name like one in another case, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", is sent.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose values flatten to the same name twice;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose timestamp falls outside the years 1 to 9999, which TelemetryDeck can’t parse;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose JSON is over 333,333 bytes. TelemetryDeck refuses the whole request for a signal over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1,000,000 bytes as its server writes it, which may be larger than the encoder’s; a third leaves","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"room for the escapes a re-encoder commonly adds.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The destination reports each as "},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckEncodingError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". When the destination is made, it logs a notice for each event and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property of the plan whose name would be left out."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"What TelemetryDeck doesn’t report","level":3,"anchor":"What-TelemetryDeck-doesnt-report","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TelemetryDeck answers 200 to any namespace and any app ID it can read, so a typo in either loses"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every signal without an error. Check that the first signals show up in the dashboard, in Test Mode"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"testMode"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TelemetryDeck doesn’t remove duplicates. A record is sent more than once when a request is retried"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after TelemetryDeck stored it but the answer was lost, when a delivery sends a cancelled batch"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again, and when a store redelivers records after a relaunch, and TelemetryDeck counts each copy."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what TelemetryDeck receives, and why, in more detail."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://TelemetryDeckEncoding/documentation/TelemetryDeckEncoding/TelemetryDeckEncodingError":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TelemetryDeckEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"TelemetryDeckEncodingError","url":"\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding\/telemetrydeckencodingerror","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TelemetryDeckEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Why ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requests as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends nothing for the batch.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckEncodingError"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder","title":"BatchEncoder","abstract":[{"text":"What turns a batch of records into the requests ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","isActive":true},{"text":" sends.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","title":"HTTPDestinations"},"doc://TelemetryDeckEncoding/documentation/TelemetryDeckEncoding/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder":{"role":"symbol","title":"TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder","abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":" of TelemetryDeck’s Ingest API v3, so an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can send events to an organization’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/v3\/<namespace>\/"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding\/telemetrydeckbatchencoder","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder","type":"topic"},"doc://TelemetryDeckEncoding/documentation/TelemetryDeckEncoding/TelemetryDeckSetupError":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Why ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder\/init(appID:testMode:plan:limit:)","isActive":true},{"text":" couldn’t be made.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding\/telemetrydecksetuperror","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TelemetryDeckSetupError","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TelemetryDeckSetupError","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckSetupError","title":"TelemetryDeckSetupError"},"doc://TelemetryDeckEncoding/documentation/TelemetryDeckEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:backoff:clock:)":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/telemetrydeck(appid:namespace:testmode:plan:backoff:clock:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:backoff:clock:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"telemetryDeck"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"appID"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","